body:
What about

```js
search.addWidget(
  instantsearch.widgets.hitsPerPageSelector({
    container: '#hits-per-page-selector',
    options: [
      {value: 10, label: '10 results'},
      {value: 50, label: '50 results'},
      {value: 100, label: '100 results'},
    ]
  })
);
```

This would map `<select><option></option></select>` and avoid repeating `hitsPerPage`.

Hmm but indexSelector has a similar approach, either we do as you proposed, or we also rename indexSelector.

Both are select so maybe we should have `options`, `value` and `text` for both of them, would be easier?
